  "body": "From #241's aside (user report): \"for the selection of the edges of the cutout, it would be helpful to have a box selector to select them as a group rather than have to click them individually.\"\n\nOn the issue's part, the top face is rimmed by 57 edge chains (corners split the chains: 4 on the outer rim, 9 on each of the 6 cutouts). Today each chain is a separate Ctrl+click, or a Shift+click per whole loop.\n\nWanted: drag a rectangle in the viewport to add every pickable feature edge (and optionally faces) inside it to the current operation's geometry pick list. The pick goes through the same undoable `SetOperationGeometry` command the click picks use, and the #692 pick rule applies (feature edges only, never tessellation edges or hidden geometry). The MCP side either gets a matching tool (pick by XY box) or a filed `MCP:` follow-up.\n\nDone means: a box drag over the cutouts part picks the rim chains inside the box in one undo step; a pinning UI test covers it; the MCP tool or its follow-up issue exists.\n\nPart of #241 (split out; the #241 fix covers the generation failures only).\n",
